runs \code{\link[=validate_phenotype_cov_block]{validate_phenotype_cov_block()}} inside its transaction before any row
is deleted, so a rejected declaration never leaves a half-written block.

The rules, from \code{plans/sample_correlated_effects.md}:
\itemize{
\item \strong{D1 — a block is declared in one call, as a complete matrix.} For a call
over phenotypes \code{N}, let \code{U} be \code{N} plus every member of every existing
block that touches \code{N}. The call is accepted only when \code{N == U}; a fragment
or a strict subset of an existing block is an error naming the omitted
